# Every file under an evidence artifacts/ directory is a write-once, hash-suffixed
# snapshot - a manifest, a test-results XML, a captured log, a human-validation
# transcript, a script or write-up committed as a record of what ran, never edited
# after the fact. Any of them reads as 100% "trailing whitespace" to git's own
# whitespace check under core.autocrlf=true merely for being wholly new in a diff -
# first found on NSC-124's .json manifest, reproduced again on its .xml results file
# the same evening, on the exact commit that introduced each, against its own
# immediate parent, nothing else in the range. Exempting the whole artifacts/ tree
# once, rather than the next extension every time a different evidence file happens
# to be newest, is the fix; there is no hygiene value in linting a frozen record.
Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/**/artifacts/** -whitespace

# Preserve vendored distribution bytes, including their original line endings.
# The upstream files contain intentional whitespace that we do not edit.
Assets/Plugins/Demigiant/DOTween/** -text -whitespace
Assets/Plugins/Demigiant/DOTween.meta -text -whitespace
Assets/Plugins/deVoid/Signals/Signals.cs -text -whitespace
Assets/Plugins/deVoid/Signals/LICENSE.txt -text -whitespace

# Unity's own YAML serializer writes "key: " (colon, one trailing space) for every
# empty-string field - m_Name, m_EditorClassIdentifier, userData, assetBundleName,
# and more - in every scene, prefab and serialized asset it saves. Confirmed real,
# not an autocrlf artifact (the committed blob genuinely has the trailing byte,
# unlike the evidence-tree case above) and confirmed ubiquitous (present across
# many already-stable scenes, not just newly-touched ones) before writing this.
# Editing it out is not an option - Unity rewrites it identically on next save,
# and hand-editing scene/prefab YAML is already forbidden elsewhere in this repo's
# own rules for the same reason: the risk is in the file, not in this exemption.
# whitespace=-blank-at-eol matches the precedent already set below for one
# DoorPrototype .meta subtree (same cause, same fix, found independently) -
# generalized here to the seven extensions Unity actually uses this format for
# under Assets/, replacing that narrower rule rather than duplicating it.
*.unity whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.prefab whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.asset whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.meta whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.anim whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.controller whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.mat whitespace=-blank-at-eol
*.inputactions whitespace=-blank-at-eol

